ployer must advertise, review applications, and interview candidates."}]," ","— ","Correct. The hiring search itself is the first cost the author names."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"A certificate earned on company time belongs to the employee."}]," ","— ","This supports the employee's gain in paragraph 4, not the cost of replacement."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"There is a period during which a new hire is still learning the job."}]," ","— ","Correct. The weeks or months of learning are the second cost the author names."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["D","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"A warehouse may add inventory software."}]," ","— ","An example used in the skills-gap argument in paragraph 3, unrelated to replacement cost."]}]]}]]]}]]}]
36:["$","details","me-p5",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",5]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"In two or three sentences, summarize the passage. State the main idea first, then the reasons the author gives. Do not include your own opinion."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-teal-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-800","children":["Model response:"," "]}],"Employer-paid training is best understood as a practical trade rather than generosity. Employers pay for it because replacing a worker is expensive and because they often cannot hire people who already have the specific skills they need. Employees gain a credential that belongs to them and can be used with a future employer."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"A strong summary leads with the trade, names both of the employer's reasons, and names the employee's gain — without adding a judgment the author did not make."]}],"$undefined"]}]]}]
37:["$","section","me-challenge",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Challenge"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","details","me-c1",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",1]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"Which statement best expresses the main idea of the passage?"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["Correct answer:"," "]}],"C. Missed appointments are largely a logistical problem, and treating them that way reduces them more effectively than treating them as a personal failing."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"No sentence states the main idea outright, so you have to build it. Paragraph 2 establishes the causes as logistical, paragraph 4 shows logistical fixes working, and paragraph 5 names the general principle. Choice C is the sentence all five paragraphs are supporting."]}],[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Every choice, explained"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["A","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Patients who miss medical appointments are not taking their health seriously."}]," ","— ","Contradicted by the text. Paragraph 2 says directly that the reasons are not indifference."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Emergency room care is more expensive than a routine clinic visit."}]," ","— ","True and stated in paragraph 3, but far too narrow. It is one detail inside the shared-cost argument."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Missed appointments are largely a logistical problem, and treating them that way reduces them more effectively than treating them as a personal failing."}]," ","— ","Correct. It covers the causes, the shared costs, the interventions that work, and the closing principle."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["D","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Clinics should send text-message reminders to every patient."}]," ","— ","Too narrow. Text reminders are one item in a list of measures in paragraph 4, not the author's point."]}]]}]]]}]]}],["$","details","me-c2",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":["$L3c","$L3d"]}],"$L3e"]}]]}]
38:["$","$L28","me-m3",{"question":{"id":"me-m3","type":"multiple-choice","question":"The example of the worker with twelve hours on Monday is included mainly to —","passageId":"me-mastery-p1","choices":["show that long shifts are common in some industries","argue that the federal threshold is unfair","demonstrate how the weekly threshold works in a case where a daily rule would give a different result","prove that most workers are underpaid"],"correctAnswer":2,"explanation":"The example exists to make the weekly-versus-daily distinction concrete: a twelve-hour day with only thirty weekly hours produces no federal overtime.","choiceRationales":["The passage says nothing about which industries have long shifts.","The passage explains the rule without judging it.","Correct. That is precisely the confusion the example is chosen to clear up.","Not in the text. No claim is made about how many workers are underpaid."],"skill":"main-ideas","difficulty":"TABE Ready"},"number":3}]
39:["$","$L28","me-m4",{"question":{"id":"me-m4","type":"multiple-choice","question":"Which of these would be the best summary of the passage?","passageId":"me-mastery-p1","choices":["Overtime is confusing and workers deserve better protection than they currently receive.","Federal overtime generally begins after forty hours in a week rather than eight hours in a day, though some states add daily rules; recognizing which rule applies is how a worker spots an underpayment.","A worker who works twelve hours on Monday and six hours on three other days has worked thirty hours.","Overtime rules are frequently misunderstood by the people they protect."],"correctAnswer":1,"explanation":"A summary states the main idea and the details it depends on, in neutral language. Choice B gives the rule, the exception, and why it matters.","choiceRationales":["Adds an opinion the author never expresses. A summary does not editorialize.","Correct. Complete, neutral, and it covers the whole paragraph.","This restates one example. A summary is not a single detail.","This is the opening sentence, and it covers only the setup — not the correction or the consequence."],"skill":"main-ideas","difficulty":"TABE Ready"},"number":4}]
3a:["$","$L28","me-p4",{"question":{"id":"me-p4","type":"multiple-select","question":"Select the TWO details the author uses to support the claim that replacing an employee is expensive.","passageId":"me-practice-training","choices":["The employer must advertise, review applications, and interview candidates.","A certificate earned on company time belongs to the employee.","There is a period during which a new hire is still learning the job.","A warehouse may add inventory software."],"correctAnswer":[0,2],"explanation":"Paragraph 2 supports the cost claim with two things: the work of running a hiring search, and the ramp-up period before a new hire is productive.","choiceRationales":["Correct. The hiring search itself is the first cost the author names.","This supports the employee's gain in paragraph 4, not the cost of replacement.","Correct. The weeks or months of learning are the second cost the author names.","An example used in the skills-gap argument in paragraph 3, unrelated to replacement cost."],"skill":"main-ideas","difficulty":"TABE Ready"},"number":4}]
3b:["$","$L28","me-p5",{"question":{"id":"me-p5","type":"short-response","question":"In two or three sentences, summarize the passage. State the main idea first, then the reasons the author gives. Do not include your own opinion.","passageId":"me-practice-training","explanation":"A strong summary leads with the trade, names both of the employer's reasons, and names the employee's gain — without adding a judgment the author did not make.","sampleResponse":"Employer-paid training is best understood as a practical trade rather than generosity. Employers pay for it because replacing a worker is expensive and because they often cannot hire people who already have the specific skills they need. Employees gain a credential that belongs to them and can be used with a future employer.","skill":"main-ideas","difficulty":"TABE Ready"},"number":5}]
3c:["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",2]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"Which detail best supports the idea that the costs of a missed appointment are shared rather than borne by the patient alone?"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}]
3d:["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["Correct answer:"," "]}],"B. The clinic loses a slot it cannot refill, which pushes the next available appointment further out for everyone else."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"The claim is that the cost is shared. This detail traces the cost outward from the patient to the clinic and then to every other patient waiting for an appointment."]}],[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Every choice, explained"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["A","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Patients cite transportation, work schedules, and child care as reasons for missing appointments."}]," ","— ","Explains why appointments are missed, not who absorbs the cost."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"The clinic loses a slot it cannot refill, which pushes the next available appointment further out for everyone else."}]," ","— ","Correct. It names a second party (the clinic) and a third (other patients), which is exactly what a shared cost means."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Some patients cannot call a clinic during business hours."}]," ","— ","Supports the argument for online rescheduling in paragraph 4, not the shared-cost claim."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["D","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"A no-show is recorded as a single line in a scheduling system."}]," ","— ","Background from paragraph 1 about how the event is recorded, not about its cost."]}]]}]]]}]
3e:["$","details","me-c3",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",3]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"Summarize the passage in three or four sentences. Include the author's explanation of why missed appointments happen and what actually reduces them."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-teal-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-800","children":["Model response:"," "]}],"Missed medical appointments are usually recorded as no-shows, but patients report that the causes are transportation, work schedules, and child care rather than indifference. The costs are shared: the clinic loses an appointment slot, the patient loses continuity of care, and the health system pays more when a manageable condition later becomes an emergency. Clinics reduce no-shows most successfully through logistical measures such as reminders, extended hours, transportation help, and online rescheduling. The author argues that treating the behavior as a logistical problem rather than a personal failing is what produces results."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"A complete summary covers the causes, the shared costs, the measures that work, and the broader principle in the final paragraph — the part most summaries leave out."]}],"$undefined"]}]]}]
